<section id="about" class="about">
  <h2 class="sec-h">About</h2>
  <p>I build the backend parts of software that people only notice when they break, and I try hard to make sure they don't.</p>
  <p>
    For seven years that meant <strong>Vocera's clinical communication platform</strong>: the APIs, message
    queues and Linux servers that get alerts and calls to hospital staff. I started there as an intern in 2014
    and left in 2021 as a platform developer and scrum master for an international team.
  </p>
  <p>
    Now I take freelance work and build small things I want to exist: a companion app for Heartopia players,
    a randomizer for Marvel Rivals lobbies, a lunch picker for coworkers who can never decide.
  </p>
  <p>
    I also teach English to students from five to sixty-five. Planning a lesson and designing an API turn out
    to be the same job: know who is in front of you and give them the right abstraction.
  </p>
</section>
